{
  "title": "MTP Dislocations",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/foot-and-ankle/7053/mtp-dislocations",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Sep 4 2023",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "MTP Dislocations are conditions characterized by multiplanar instability of the MTP joint which may present as as a \"crossover toe.\"",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with presence of dorsomedial deviation of the toe in relation to the metatarsal.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment consists of a trial of shoe modifications, and taping. Operative management is indicated for patients with progressive pain and fixed deformities.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathoanatomic stages",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**plantar plate disrupted**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "can be caused by",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "traumatic rupture",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "chronic inflammation (more common)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**lateral collateral ligament fails**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "leads to medial deviation of the second toe",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "plantar plate, with its flexor tendon attachments, displace medially",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "medial displacement of the proximal phalanx relative to the metatarsal",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**medial structures become contracted**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "lumbrical and interosseous tendons, medial collateral ligament (MCL), and medial capsule become tight and contracted creating adduction force",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**plantar plate subsequently fails**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "hyperextension forces on the proximal phalanx result in dorsal instability",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "MTP synovitis, deformity often accelerated by cortisone injection done for either misdiagnosed Morton's neuroma or into the MPJ for synovitis.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Plantar plate",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "anatomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "broad, thick ligamentous structure that spans the plantar aspect of the MTP joint",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/7053/images/plantar%20plate.jpg",
                      "caption": "Cross section of cadaveric MTP joint showing plantar plate (black arrow)"
                    },
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/7053/images/mri%20plantar%20plate.jpg",
                      "caption": "Sagittal MRI showing structures at MTP joint. Plantar plate inserts on the metatarsal head (curved arrow) and the proximal phalanx (black arrow head)"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "origin",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "on the metatarsal head via a thin synovial attachment, just proximal to the metatarsal articular surface",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "insertion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "plantar base of the proximal phalanx",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "function",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "resists tensile loads in the sagittal plane (particularly in dorsiflexion of the joint)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "cushion the joint and support weightbearing forces",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "walking on “marble in the ball of their foot”",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "early instability (prior to deformity) may be confused with Morton's neuroma, deformity often follows cortisone injection for presumed neuroma",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "callus under the metatarsal head",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "dorsomedial deviation of the toe in relation to the metatarsal",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "hammertoe (flexion at the PIPJ, extension at the MPJ)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "dorsal instability found on modified Lachman test",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "grip toe (proximal phalanx) with one hand and the metatarsal head with the other and move toe dorsally",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "weightbearing AP, oblique, and lateral",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP shows dislocation of the proximal phalanx (medial more often than lateral)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "weightbearing lateral shows hyperextension and dorsal dislocation of the proximal phalanx",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "rule out other pathology",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "elucidate pathology of surrounding structures",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "used in early stages of MTP synovitis to evaluate plantar plate but not necessarily useful in dislocation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "taping, shoe modification, metatarsal pads, Budin splint, and NSAIDS",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "first line of treatment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "will not correct deformity",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "distal oblique shortening MT osteotomy (Weil procedure)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "significant pain and loss of function",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "fixed deformity",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "plantar plate repair",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "performed with metatarsal osteotomy",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "sutures passed through distal plantar plate and then through drill holes in proximal phalanx",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "flexor to extensor tendon transfer",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "FDL split and brought over top of proximal phalanx to stabilize joint",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "EDB transfer under intermetatarsal ligament",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Distal oblique shortening MT osteotomy (Weil procedure)**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "soft tissue balancing",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "dorsal and medial capsular release with lateral capsular reefing can be used in combination with Weil osteotomy",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "EDB tendon transfer after rerouting tendon through transverse intermetatarsal ligament results in a dynamic stabilizer of incompetent lateral structures",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "flexor digitorum longus (FDL)–to–extensor digitorum longus (EDL) tendon transfer (Girdlestone-Taylor procedure)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "resection arthroplasty of the metatarsal head (DuVries)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "plantar plate repair as above",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "osteotomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "intra-articular osteotomy that achieves longitudinal decompression through shortening and allows joint reduction.",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "metatarsal (MT) is exposed and the direction of shortening in the original Weil procedure runs mostly parallel to the plantar aspect of the foot.",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "fixation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "osteotomy is fixed by means of a screw running perpendicular to the osteotomy line.",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Floating toe deformity**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "inability to flex MTP joint causing 2nd digit dorsiflexion deformity (ie. floating toe)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "most common complication",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Toe vascular compromise**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "if correcting a chronic dislocation, the soft tissue (including vasculature) can contract",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "stretching of the vasculature can compromise flow",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "procedure may need to be reversed to save digit",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
